    "knowledge_point": "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/assets/883d270ae063f134ee0ac04f717bcc9b5800adb939be3c7f19f25602ad52360e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-2\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-2$ and *below* the line $y=2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-2,\\,y<2.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-2<y<2.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=2$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n-2<y\\le 2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<y\\le 2}.\n$$",
